+(durations)=
+
+### Durations
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a string such as `1h30m` into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. A value is one or more
+`<integer><unit>` parts, using the units `d`, `h`, `m`, `s`, and `ms`. The parts must be in that order, largest unit
+first, and each unit may be used at most once. A bare integer is a number of seconds. Negative values, signs, and
+whitespace are not accepted.
+
+`min` and `max` are optional {class}`datetime.timedelta` values. Like {class}`IntRange`, they are inclusive, and an
+omitted side is unbounded.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration())
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(timeout.total_seconds())
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=2h'])
+```
+
